.\" Title: vrunner-screenshot
.\" Author: vrunner contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\" Process this file with
.\"   groff -man -Tascii vrunner-screenshot.1

.TH VRUNNER-SCREENSHOT 1 "2025" "vrunner" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrunner screenshot \- capture the VTTY buffer as a PNG screenshot

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrunner screenshot
[\fITARGET\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Captures the virtual terminal (VTTY) buffer of a running command and renders it as a PNG image using a TrueType/OpenType font. The screenshot includes the visible screen content with all ANSI colors, bold, underline, and other formatting preserved.

The rendering engine uses \fBfontdue\fR for font rasterization with proper baseline alignment, supporting 256-color and true-color output, CJK wide characters, box-drawing characters, and bold overstrike emulation.

When no target is specified and exactly one command is running, that command is selected automatically. If multiple commands are running, a target must be specified either by PID (numeric) or by command name.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-\-output \fIFILE\fR
Output file path for the PNG image (default: \fBscreenshot.png\fR).

.TP
.BR \-\-font-size \fIN\fR
Font size in pixels per character cell (default: \fB14\fR, valid range: 6\[en]48). Smaller values produce more compact screenshots; larger values produce higher-resolution output suitable for presentations or documentation.

.TP
.BR \-\-font-name \fIPATH\fR
Path to a TTF/OTF font file (e.g., \fB./SGr-IosevkaTerm-Medium.ttc\fR). When omitted, the server searches common system paths for a monospace font: \fBDejaVuSansMono.ttf\fR, \fBLiberationMono-Regular.ttf\fR, and \fBFreeMono.ttf\fR.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and exit.

.SH TARGET SELECTION

If \fITARGET\fR is provided:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
Numeric values are treated as a process ID (PID).
.IP \(bu 4
Non-numeric values are matched case-insensitively against command names.
.RE

If no \fITARGET\fR is provided and exactly one command is running, it is selected automatically. If multiple commands are running, an error is printed listing available commands.

.SH RENDERING DETAILS

The PNG renderer uses the font's horizontal line metrics for correct baseline alignment:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
\fBcell_width\fR is derived from the font's advance width for a typical character.
.IP \(bu 4
\fBcell_height\fR is computed from the font's \fBascent\fR and \fBdescent\fR metrics.
.IP \(bu 4
All glyphs are positioned relative to a shared baseline using the font's \fBbearing_y\fR (top sidebearing) and \fBymin\fR (bottom edge) metrics, ensuring characters with and without descenders align correctly.
.IP \(bu 4
Bold text is rendered with a 1-pixel overstrike to the right.
.IP \(bu 4
Underline and strikethrough are rendered as pixel lines.
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES

Capture a screenshot with default settings:
.RS
.PP
\fB$ vrunner screenshot\fR
.RE

Specify output path and custom font:
.RS
.PP
\fB$ vrunner screenshot \-\-output /tmp/term.png \-\-font-name ./SGr-IosevkaTerm-Medium.ttc\fR
.RE

Use a large font for high-resolution output:
.RS
.PP
\fB$ vrunner screenshot \-\-font-size 20 \-\-output screenshot-hires.png\fR
.RE

Target a specific command:
.RS
.PP
\fB$ vrunner screenshot htop \-\-output htop-capture.png\fR
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vrunner (1),
.BR vrunner-cat (1),
